<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!-- N°COMMAND R23 command vehicle, deployed, as on the R23 render on Symphony's landing page
     (public/landing/r23-seq): a Toyota Hilux Double Cab in olive drab with a darker canopy over the bed (N°COMMAND
     on its rear face), the canopy roof slid back 1.5 m, both side panels opened flat, the main cassettes slid out
     1 m and the outer extensions 0.88 m beyond them, eight landing pads, the hexa in its bay, a snorkel.
     Frame and dimensions are Symphony's (src/components/hud/vehicle/PanggungR23.tsx, R23 constants; CAD frame:
     metres, Z up, Y towards the rear, X to the vehicle's left, model origin on the ground under the front
     bumper's centre). Pad centres (deck top z = 1.095):
       main left (+1.42, 4.115) (+1.42, 4.905)   main right (-1.42, 4.115) (-1.42, 4.905)
       outer left (+2.30, 4.115) (+2.30, 4.905)  outer right (-2.30, 4.115) (-2.30, 4.905)
     Meshes: symphony/convert_r23.mjs from Symphony public/models/r23; parts, colours and textures:
     symphony/texture_r23.py (*_tex.obj with .mtl, materials/textures for the boxes).
     Collisions are boxes: an OBJ mesh as a collision shape crashes DART's Bullet detector.
     Body: "2026 Toyota Hilux" by missyubibi attage, CC-BY-4.0
       https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/2026-toyota-hilux-9743da567da24663a92c33619fe06746 -->
<sdf version="1.9">
